{"availability":"available","full":"chemerisuk/better-dom","name":"better-dom","description":"Live extension playground","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":544,"forks":32,"created":"2013-01-06T11:49:47Z","updated":"2020-03-24T09:56:54Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"http://chemerisuk.github.io/better-dom/","topics":[],"demo":"http://chemerisuk.github.io/better-dom/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T11:01:37.179Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T11:01:37.179Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T11:01:37.179Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T09:01:35.951Z","stars":544,"forks":32},{"at":"2026-10-17T11:01:37.179Z","stars":544,"forks":32}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[][npm-url] [][travis-url] [][coveralls-url] [][npm-url] [][twitter-url]","This library is about ideas. After some time of using jQuery I found that it's just too big, has lack of features needed and the API design is debatable. In particular live extensions was one of the main ideas that encouraged me to build a new library from scratch.","Vanilla DOM also has a lot of bad parts, that I'm trying to fix by providing a JavaScript wrapper for each DOM element you use in code. This extra layer allows to abstract from legacy interfaces and to add new methods on the top of particular elements without touching vanilla DOM prototypes. So the object model used is very different from what jQuery does."],"features":["lightweight: 5 kB gzipped","declarative animations","improved event handling"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chemerisuk/better-dom/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"ab4090b13119e900f7494ee78e025422d6ba510807b1eaaa8c5c07cd7c55febe","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:36.048Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:36.048Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"[][npm-url] [][travis-url] [][coveralls-url] [][npm-url] [][twitter-url]","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chemerisuk/better-dom/blob/master